A first date on a Ferris wheel in Geelong sparked a romance that came full circle six years later with a proposal on another! For Aishwarya Sanjay and Samuel Welsh, the next chapter was a wedding that brought together their South Indian and Australian roots.

Their celebration was filled with personal touches, from a vibrant garden of orange marigolds to bespoke prints featuring the Indian peacock and Australian kookaburra. From finding love under the stars to a lifelong flower-bedecked promise, here's looking at how this couple's two-culture wedding was the best of both worlds! 

